From b9263596c5d8c29d7675c65d87d7d66efee60910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vonsek <45567075+Vonsek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:44:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] rdna2spirv: ds_append and ds_consume (LDS)

One add / subtract of the wave's active-lane count at the offset address,
done by the first active lane; the old value to every active lane by a
subgroup shuffle (an exchange round under --wave64-emulate). Measured
natively on gfx1036: the offset alone is the address, M0 does not move it.
The gds form stays Unsupported. GPU fixtures cs_w32/w64_ds_append, semantic
test test_ds_append.py, design.md row.

AI-assisted.
